---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "./PageHeader.astro";
import PostList from "./PostList.astro";
import Pager from "./Pager.astro";
import type { Post } from "../lib/posts";
interface Props { posts: Post[]; page: number; totalPages: number }
const { posts, page, totalPages } = Astro.props;
---

<BaseLayout title="Gurbaaz Singh" description="Welcome to my homepage. Hope you enjoy!">
  <PageHeader title="Gurbaaz Singh" subtitle="Welcome to my homepage. Hope you enjoy!" />
  <div class="content-column page-content">
    <p>If you stumbled upon this link and are currently reading this, high chances are you got redirected here from one of my socials, or you are a friend / relative / professor / company recruiter with whom I have shared this link at some point in time of my life. There is also a very low but possible chance of you being a web crawler (<em>data is the new oil</em>), a stalker or just a random admirer. Whatever it is, you are welcome here.<br /><br /></p>
    <p>Find your way around. For starters, you can go through my <a class="post-disable-highlight" href="/blog/"><u>posts</u></a>, or get to know more about me <a class="post-disable-highlight" href="/aboutme/"><u>here</u></a>.<br /><br /></p>
    <p>See ya!</p>
    <hr class="small" />
    <PostList posts={posts} />
    {totalPages > 1 && <Pager previous={page > 1 ? { url: page === 2 ? "/" : `/page${page - 1}/`, label: "← Newer Posts" } : undefined} next={page < totalPages ? { url: `/page${page + 1}/`, label: "Older Posts →" } : undefined} />}
    <ul class="pagination blog-pager"><li><a class="page-link" href="/blog/">View all posts →</a></li></ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
